<h2>If none of those four answers fit</h2>

<p>A pre-built plan assumes your week looks like the average week. If you travel often, if you're coming back from injury, or if your availability changes month to month, no plan in the catalog will quite fit — and forcing one is worse than not using it.</p>

<p>That's where 1:1 coaching makes sense: same method, but the plan is built around your actual week and adjusted when it changes. There are also <a href="/en/#planes">other distances</a> if the marathon isn't the right race this cycle.</p>
